24:["$","$L36",null,{"faqs":[{"question":"How much does it cost to develop a mobile app?","answer":"Most custom apps run from about $30K for a focused MVP to $250K+ for a complex, multi-feature product, driven by the number of screens, integrations, and platforms. Cross-platform development usually cuts the cost of covering both iOS and Android roughly in half. We scope a fixed number after a short discovery, so you're not signing a blank check."},{"question":"Cross-platform vs native — which is right for my app?","answer":"For most business apps, cross-platform (React Native or Flutter) is the better choice: one codebase ships to both stores, costs less, and is easier to maintain. Native (Swift/Kotlin) wins when you need maximum performance or deep device features — games, AR, heavy hardware use. We recommend based on your app and budget, not a default."},{"question":"How long does it take to build a mobile app?","answer":"A focused MVP is typically a few months; a full product with backend and integrations takes longer. Cross-platform shortens it because you build once for both stores. We start with a discovery to scope the MVP, then ship in iterations so you see a working app early instead of waiting for a big-bang launch."},{"question":"Do you build for both iOS and Android?","answer":"Yes. We build cross-platform apps that run on both iOS and Android from a single codebase, or native apps for each platform when that's the right call. Either way, we handle the App Store and Google Play differences, so your app works and ships on both."},{"question":"Do you handle App Store and Google Play submission?","answer":"Yes — submission, review, and compliance are part of the job. We prepare the store listings, handle Apple and Google review guidelines, and manage the launch, so you don't get stuck in rejection loops. We also set up app store optimization (ASO) and analytics so the app can actually get downloaded."},{"question":"Do you maintain the app after launch?","answer":"Yes, and it matters — apps that aren't maintained break on the next OS update. We offer ongoing maintenance: OS-version support, bug fixes, and new features over time. And because we're nearshore and you own the codebase, you're never locked in or waiting 12 hours for a fix."},{"question":"What's included in your mobile app development services?","answer":"Our mobile app development services cover the full lifecycle: UX and product design, cross-platform or native builds for iOS and Android, the backend and APIs behind the app, App Store and Google Play submission, and ongoing maintenance through every OS update. You get one nearshore team from idea to installed, not a design shop and a separate dev shop stitched together. At the end, the codebase and the store accounts are yours."},{"question":"How do I choose a cross-platform app development company?","answer":"Pick a cross-platform app development company that ships to both stores from one React Native or Flutter codebase, hands you the source code, and maintains the app after launch instead of disappearing at handoff. Ask whether the backend and store submission are included, and check the time-zone gap: a nearshore team in US hours iterates the same day, while offshore adds a 12-hour lag. WeEvolveIT covers all of it, nearshore from Monterrey, with 1,000+ projects across 17 countries in 15+ years."},{"question":"What frameworks do you use for cross-platform app development?","answer":"We build cross-platform apps in React Native and Flutter, the two frameworks that ship a single codebase to both iOS and Android. React Native fits apps that share logic with a React web product; Flutter fits highly custom, animation-heavy interfaces. When an app needs maximum performance or deep hardware access, we go native in Swift and Kotlin instead, and we recommend based on your app, not a house default."}],"id":"faq","title":"What teams ask about building an app.","fill":true}]
